<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Initial preventive physical examination completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and the prevention plan made. Pneumococcal conjugate, first recombinant zoster, Tdap and first hepatitis B vaccine doses given; colorectal cancer screening ordered; prostate cancer screening discussed and declined; vision, hearing, falls and cognition screened without concern. [S]<list><item>Second hepatitis B vaccine dose in about eight weeks, at the twelve-week visit.</item><item>Second zoster vaccine dose in two to six months.</item><item>Community dental clinic referral for the loose teeth.</item><item>Annual wellness visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Stage 2 hypertension (I10)</content>. Improving two weeks after starting two drugs: office 144/86, home average 142/86; target below 130/80. Tolerating the medicines. [S]<list><item>Continue hydrochlorothiazide 25 mg and amlodipine 5 mg; electrolytes and creatinine at the six-week visit, as planned.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Re-entry after incarceration (Z65.2)</content>. Room secured by the week; benefits applications in progress with the social worker. [S]<list><item>Continue with the social worker on a longer lease and benefits.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Blood pressure</td><td>Completed today</td><td>144/86 mmHg; treated hypertension</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-2 score 1; PHQ-9 7 at intake</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco use</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Never used tobacco</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy alcohol use</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No alcohol</td></tr><tr><td>Colorectal cancer screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Never screened; he chose a yearly fecal immunochemical test; kit given</td></tr><tr><td>Prostate cancer screening</td><td>Declined</td><td>Shared decision about PSA screening at 55 to 69; after hearing the benefits and harms he chose not to be screened</td></tr><tr><td>Abdominal aortic aneurysm screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Never smoked and no family history recorded</td></tr><tr><td>Lung cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Never smoked</td></tr><tr><td>Cholesterol and cardiovascular risk</td><td>Up to date</td><td>LDL 148 mg/dL at intake; on atorvastatin 40 mg for carotid atherosclerosis</td></tr><tr><td>Diabetes</td><td>Up to date</td><td>HbA1c 5.5% and fasting glucose 94 mg/dL at intake</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis C screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Antibody nonreactive at intake (signal-to-cutoff 0.08); repeat only with new risk</td></tr><tr><td>Latent tuberculosis screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Interferon-gamma release assay negative at intake; no cough, fever or weight loss</td></tr><tr><td>HIV screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Nonreactive at intake</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B screening and vaccination</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Panel at intake negative for infection and immunity; CpG-adjuvanted hepatitis B vaccine dose 1 of 2 today, recommended at 60 or older with a risk factor such as incarceration</td></tr><tr><td>Pneumococcal vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PCV20 today; no further dose needed</td></tr><tr><td>Zoster vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Recombinant zoster vaccine dose 1 of 2 today</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus, diphtheria, and pertussis</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Tdap today; no records of earlier doses</td></tr><tr><td>Influenza vaccine</td><td>Due</td><td>High-dose or adjuvanted vaccine in the autumn</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine</td><td>Declined</td><td>Current vaccine offered for adults 65 or older; he declined for now and will reconsider in the autumn</td></tr><tr><td>Vision</td><td>Completed today</td><td>20/30 in each eye with glasses; optometry for new glasses</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Whispered voice test normal</td></tr><tr><td>Falls risk</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No falls; timed up-and-go 9 seconds</td></tr><tr><td>Cognitive screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Mini-Cog 5 of 5; no concerns</td></tr><tr><td>Oral health</td><td>Referred</td><td>Community dental clinic for two loose molars; not covered by Medicare</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Pneumococcal conjugate vaccine (PCV20); Recombinant zoster vaccine, dose 1 of 2; Tdap vaccine; Hepatitis B vaccine, CpG-adjuvanted (two-dose series), dose 1 of 2 [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: 2025 AHA/ACC/AANP/AAPA/ABC/ACCP/ACPM/AGS/AMA/ASPC/NMA/PCNA/SGIM Guideline for the Prevention, Detection, Evaluation and Management of High Blood Pressure in Adults (Jones DW, et al. Hypertension 2025;82:e212-e316) (2025); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026); Adult Immunization Schedule by Age (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Six-week review in two weeks, with electrolytes and creatinine. Next scheduled visit 2026-08-18: six-week review: blood pressure, electrolytes and kidney function on hydrochlorothiazide and amlodipine; statin and aspirin tolerance. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.21" extension="2015-08-01"/>
    <code code="42348-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Advance directives"/>
    <title>Advance Care Planning</title>
    <text><paragraph>Voluntary advance care planning discussion of about 20 minutes, with his consent. He named a health care agent, a friend he trusts, and a health care proxy form was completed; the agent is recorded in the chart and is not named here. He would want full treatment for a stroke or heart attack, including clot-dissolving treatment and rehabilitation, and he would not want to be kept alive by machines if he could no longer think or write. The plan will be revisited at his annual wellness visit or after any serious illness. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>
